1
00:00:06,178 --> 00:00:08,476
Whiskers and the Flying Trunk.

2
00:00:17,943 --> 00:00:21,967
One grey, rainy evening, nobody felt cosy at all.

3
00:00:22,167 --> 00:00:25,997
Rain, rain, rain. And my blanket is in the wash.

4
00:00:31,758 --> 00:00:35,539
Look! Fairy tales by Hans Christian Andersen, from Copenhagen!

5
00:00:35,739 --> 00:00:38,932
The Flying Trunk. Click its lock, and away it flies!

6
00:00:39,132 --> 00:00:41,613
Pah. Fairy tales aren't real. Click!

7
00:00:48,609 --> 00:00:50,669
Then let's fly! To Copenhagen!

8
00:00:59,519 --> 00:01:03,079
Over the clouds and across the sea flew the trunk.

9
00:01:10,075 --> 00:01:13,730
I'm not scared. My fur is just extra fluffy.

10
00:01:20,108 --> 00:01:22,851
Copper roofs and twisty spires! Copenhagen!

11
00:01:34,172 --> 00:01:38,096
They landed among the painted houses of the New Harbour.

12
00:01:44,474 --> 00:01:47,947
Two ducks were laughing at a scruffy grey bird.

13
00:01:52,472 --> 00:01:55,758
Yes, I know. I'm the ugliest duckling in Denmark.

14
00:01:55,958 --> 00:01:58,788
Ugly? I'm grey too. Grey is the best colour!

15
00:01:58,988 --> 00:02:01,084
Really? I'm Saga. Thank you!

16
00:02:01,284 --> 00:02:04,979
Hungry? Bodil's bakery has the best pastries in town.

17
00:02:05,179 --> 00:02:07,157
Did somebody say pastries?

18
00:02:12,918 --> 00:02:16,533
Velkommen! Try my smørrebrød. Open sandwiches!

19
00:02:22,911 --> 00:02:25,676
Excuse me. Somebody stole the lid.

20
00:02:25,876 --> 00:02:29,271
Ho ho! In Denmark, sandwiches don't have lids!

21
00:02:39,356 --> 00:02:41,289
He's turned into a cinnamon roll!

22
00:02:41,489 --> 00:02:44,640
I did that on purpose. It's a cinnamon blanket.

23
00:02:49,783 --> 00:02:51,698
Oh no! The ducks clicked the lock!

24
00:02:57,458 --> 00:02:59,570
It's heading for the palace! Follow me!

25
00:02:59,770 --> 00:03:03,615
At the palace, the royal guards wear tall bearskin hats.

26
00:03:13,082 --> 00:03:15,140
How do I look? Very royal?

27
00:03:19,665 --> 00:03:24,014
By the sea sat the Little Mermaid, from another Andersen story.

28
00:03:24,214 --> 00:03:27,744
She left the sea, but never quite fit in on land. Like me.

29
00:03:27,944 --> 00:03:31,874
I don't fit in either. Too round. But Luna likes me anyway.

30
00:03:32,074 --> 00:03:33,967
There! It's flying to Tivoli!

31
00:03:39,109 --> 00:03:42,931
At nightfall, the lanterns of Tivoli Gardens lit up.

32
00:03:50,545 --> 00:03:52,934
The trunk is stuck on the old roller coaster!

33
00:03:53,134 --> 00:03:54,415
Leave it to me.

34
00:04:08,207 --> 00:04:10,889
I missed. On purpose. To check the view.

35
00:04:11,089 --> 00:04:12,038
It's too high!

36
00:04:12,238 --> 00:04:15,045
I could try. But ugly ducklings can't fly.

37
00:04:15,245 --> 00:04:17,846
Who says you're a duckling? Spread your wings, Saga!

38
00:04:18,046 --> 00:04:19,864
Go on! We believe in you!

39
00:04:33,656 --> 00:04:36,181
She's not a duckling at all. She's a swan!

40
00:04:36,381 --> 00:04:38,179
I'm a swan? I'm a swan!

41
00:04:45,792 --> 00:04:48,900
That night, Bodil made hot cocoa for everyone.

42
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:53,358
Cosy together? We call it hooga. Spelled H, Y, G, G, E!

43
00:04:53,558 --> 00:04:55,657
Hooga. My new favourite word.

44
00:04:55,857 --> 00:04:58,910
Thank you for being my friends, even when I was scruffy.

45
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:02,397
We'll always be your friends. Grey, white, or polka-dot.

46
00:05:16,807 --> 00:05:20,127
Saga flew beside the trunk, all the way home.

47
00:05:25,887 --> 00:05:28,465
Look! The Ugly Duckling story. That's Saga!

48
00:05:28,665 --> 00:05:32,126
Fairy tales aren't real. Except the ones that are.

49
00:05:32,326 --> 00:05:33,746
Let's make hooga at home!

50
00:05:33,946 --> 00:05:37,475
A candle, cocoa, and my best friends. Perfect.

51
00:05:37,675 --> 00:05:43,679
Being different isn't being wrong. And a kind friend can help anyone find their wings.

